diff --git a/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd b/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
index 70db537..5634762 100644
--- a/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
+++ b/docs/labwc-actions.5.scd
@@ -336,6 +336,38 @@ Actions are used in menus and keyboard/mouse bindings.
 	Resizes active window size to width and height of the output when the
 	window size exceeds the output size.
 
+*<action name="PlaceOnOutput" output="DP-2" x="0" y="0" width="0" height="0" maximized="no" />*
+	Moves the window to the named output and gives it a position and size.
+	Fullscreen, maximized, snapped and shaded states are left first. If no
+	usable output has that name, the window is left where it is.
+
+	*output* Output (connector) name. Required.
+
+	*x* and *y* Position of the window, relative to the top-left corner
+	of the output. Like *width* and *height*, they describe the window
+	without server-side decorations, as the "place" of the windows reply on
+	the tiling control socket does. Default is 0.
+
+	*width* and *height* Size of the window. 0 or unset keeps its size.
+
+	A window that does not fit the usable area of the output (the output
+	without panels) is shrunk and shifted until it does.
+
+	*maximized* [yes|no] Maximize the window on that output afterwards.
+	Default is no.
+
+	A window that tiling arranges is only moved to the output; tiling then
+	places it.
+
+	As a window rule action, it runs when the window is first mapped, after
+	the initial placement:
+
+```
+<windowRule identifier="discord" type="normal" matchOnce="true">
+  <action name="PlaceOnOutput" output="DP-2" x="1620" y="40" width="900" height="1300" />
+</windowRule>
+```
+
 *<action name="GoToDesktop" to="value" wrap="yes" toggle="no" />*
 	Switch to workspace.
 
